From a3a50b9377aa6c83d9f5a1a7d6a6d024537d10f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 06:43:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 125/144] feat(pypto-x): add native AVX-512 VNNI W8A8 widening
 path

Implement contract 0002 C4 / R6 on the W8B avx512-blocked-gemm base:

- qmatmul_s8s8_s32 is wired through scalar validation -> CPU vector plan ->
  AVX-512 VNNI lowering -> artifact metadata -> runtime dispatch.  The native
  kernel uses vpdpbusd (u8 x s8) with an explicit +128 bias of the unsigned
  right operand and a signed -128 * sum_k(left_row) correction per output row:
  sum a*b = sum a*(b+128) - 128*sum a.  VPDPBUSD wraps its dword lanes modulo
  2^32 (it is not the saturating VPDPBUSDS variant) and the frozen scheme
  bounds the exact output by K*127*127 <= INT32_MAX (Q5), so the corrected
  wrapped value is bit-exact; a dedicated case covers the worst-case biased
  intermediate 255*127*K = 4,311,035,640 > INT32_MAX.
- Capability declaration travels through CapabilitySet
  (s8s8_s32_vnni_dpbusd) and is gated by the independent CPUID avx512vnni bit.
  A target without VNNI cannot lower the opcode, and the runtime entry points
  re-probe and compare the artifact declaration, so there is no widening or
  BF16 fallback and no silent downgrade.
- Probe-gated target entry points implement the remaining three opcodes
  bit-exactly against the C1 goldens: dequantize_s8, single-rounding
  dequantize_epilogue_bf16 and quantize_per_token_s8 (exact FP64 RNE semantics
  for Q1/Q2/Q4/Q5/Q6); the Core IR multi-output wiring stays in C7/C8.
- AVX-512 artifact payload 4 -> 5 and native ABI marker :5 -> :6 (the rebased
  integration base already carried the W8B blocked-gemm payload 4 / marker :5);
  old artifacts fail closed at load.  AVX2 payload 3 / marker :4 and the
  BF16/packed planes are unchanged.
- 91 new focused tests: capability/probe gate, rank-2/3/4 golden differential,
  non-multiple-of-8 tails, K upper bound and wraparound compensation cases,
  the three primitive goldens, fail-closed metadata/capability tampering, and
  objdump evidence that the shared object really emits vpdpbusd (zero
  vpdpwssd).
